From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:59:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] Enable the $XD OU Fixes cheat to match the stable
 XDNetplay bundle

The 2-year-stable papajefe Windows build enables $XD OU Fixes (ActionReplay),
with Core/EnableCheats=True and NetPlay/SyncCodes=True. Its four NOPs patch
XD's battle-setup code and the conditional at 0x80BC0E04 keys the battle mode
off 0x80475580 -- the OU GBA-vs-GBA format depends on it, and the config the
original ships expects it. Our bundle only defined the code without enabling it.

Enable it by default in the Sys game ini (respected because LoadCodes marks
codes enabled in the global/Sys layer as default_enabled), and force
Core/EnableCheats on in the launcher for both solo boot and hosting. Only this
code is enabled, not the cosmetic 60 FPS / widescreen, since 60 FPS changes
game timing and would break netplay determinism.
---
 Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini                      | 11 +++++++++++
 .../features/xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt       |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
index 6b10062..f53ccb8 100644
--- a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
+++ b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
@@ -12,6 +12,17 @@ $Allow Memory Card saving with Savestates
 [Patches_RetroAchievements_Verified]
 $Allow Memory Card saving with Savestates
 
+# Match the 2-year-stable papajefe XDNetplay Windows bundle: the $XD OU Fixes
+# AR code is ENABLED by default (its four NOPs patch XD's battle-setup code and
+# the conditional at 0x80BC0E04 keys the battle mode off 0x80475580). This is
+# required for the OU GBA-vs-GBA format to behave correctly, and the config the
+# original ships EXPECTS it. Only this code is enabled (not the cosmetic 60 FPS
+# / widescreen), because 60 FPS changes game timing and would break netplay
+# determinism. Cheats must also be globally on (Core/EnableCheats=True, set by
+# the launcher) and SyncCodes=True so the guest receives the same enabled set.
+[ActionReplay_Enabled]
+$XD OU Fixes
+
 [ActionReplay]
 $16:9 Widescreen
 044ED860 3FC962F9
diff --git a/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt b/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt
index fc31279..eefb2b6 100644
--- a/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt
+++ b/Source/Android/app/src/main/java/org/dolphinemu/dolphinemu/features/xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ import androidx.compose.runtime.setValue
 import org.dolphinemu.dolphinemu.features.netplay.ui.NetplaySetupActivity
 import java.io.File
 import java.security.MessageDigest
+import org.dolphinemu.dolphinemu.features.settings.model.BooleanSetting
 import org.dolphinemu.dolphinemu.features.settings.model.IntSetting
 import org.dolphinemu.dolphinemu.features.settings.model.NativeConfig
 import org.dolphinemu.dolphinemu.features.settings.model.StringSetting
@@ -309,6 +310,14 @@ class XDLauncherActivity : AppCompatActivity(), ThemeProvider {
         if (IntSetting.MAIN_SI_DEVICE_2.int != 13) {
             IntSetting.MAIN_SI_DEVICE_2.setInt(NativeConfig.LAYER_BASE, 13); changed = true
         }
+        // The 2-year-stable papajefe XDNetplay bundle runs with cheats ON so the
+        // $XD OU Fixes AR code (enabled in the bundled GXXE01.ini) actually
+        // applies -- it patches XD's battle-setup code and the OU GBA-vs-GBA
+        // format depends on it. Match that for both solo boot and hosting; in
+        // netplay the host's EnableCheats + SyncCodes carry it to the guest.
+        if (!BooleanSetting.MAIN_ENABLE_CHEATS.boolean) {
+            BooleanSetting.MAIN_ENABLE_CHEATS.setBoolean(NativeConfig.LAYER_BASE, true); changed = true
+        }
         if (changed) {
             NativeConfig.save(NativeConfig.LAYER_BASE)
         }
